<div class="breadcrumb"><a title="Why deepdoc?" href="../index.html">deepdoc</a> › parser</div>

<h1>Parser Module — File Format Extraction</h1>
<p>Format-specific extractors for PDF, DOCX, Excel, HTML, Markdown, JSON, Text, EPUB, and PowerPoint.</p>

<div class="hero">
<p><strong>What is this?</strong> — The parser layer handles file-format specifics: decoding PDF streams, walking DOCX XML trees, iterating Excel cells, traversing HTML DOMs. Each format gets its own extraction strategy.</p>
</div>

<div class="stat-row">
<div class="stat-box"><div class="num">18</div><div class="label">Core Parsers</div></div>
<div class="stat-box"><div class="num">200KB+</div><div class="label">Code</div></div>
<div class="stat-box"><div class="num">5</div><div class="label">Alt Engines</div></div>
</div>

<h2>Core Parsers (Format-Specific)</h2>

<div class="card-grid">
<a title="PDF Parsing Pipeline - Deepdoc Wiki" href="pdf-parsing-pipeline/index.html" class="card">
<h4>PDF Parser</h4>
<p><code>pdf_parser.py</code> (85KB) — Master handler for PDF files.</p>
<ul>
<li>Text extraction via pdfplumber</li>
<li>Layout recognition</li>
<li>Table detection & cell grid</li>
<li>Figure extraction</li>
<li>OCR fallback for scanned PDFs</li>
<li>Focus: <a title="PDF Parsing Pipeline - Deepdoc Wiki" href="pdf-parsing-pipeline/index.html">PDF Parsing Pipeline</a></li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>DOCX Parser</h4>
<p><code>docx_parser.py</code> (6.7KB) — Microsoft Word extraction via python-docx.</p>
<ul>
<li>Heading hierarchy preservation</li>
<li>Paragraph-level text grouping</li>
<li>Table extraction via XML parsing</li>
<li>Embedded image handling</li>
<li>Style metadata (bold, italic, font)</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>Excel Parser</h4>
<p><code>excel_parser.py</code> (11KB) — XLSX cell extraction and structure.</p>
<ul>
<li>Sheet enumeration</li>
<li>Merged cell handling</li>
<li>Formula vs. value detection</li>
<li>Cell type coercion (date, number, text)</li>
<li>Row/column grouping</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>HTML Parser</h4>
<p><code>html_parser.py</code> (8.3KB) — BeautifulSoup-based DOM traversal.</p>
<ul>
<li>Recursive element walking</li>
<li>Block-level vs. inline detection</li>
<li>Link extraction</li>
<li>Script/style tag filtering</li>
<li>Deep nesting unwinding</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>Markdown Parser</h4>
<p><code>markdown_parser.py</code> (12KB) — AST-based MD extraction.</p>
<ul>
<li>Heading-based sectioning</li>
<li>Code block preservation</li>
<li>List structure preservation</li>
<li>Link and image metadata</li>
<li>Blockquote hierarchies</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>JSON Parser</h4>
<p><code>json_parser.py</code> (6.4KB) — JSON and JSONL extraction.</p>
<ul>
<li>JSON tree flattening</li>
<li>JSONL line-by-line parsing</li>
<li>Key extraction strategy</li>
<li>Nested object handling</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>Text Parser</h4>
<p><code>txt_parser.py</code> (2.3KB) — Plain text with line grouping.</p>
<ul>
<li>Blank-line-based chunking</li>
<li>Paragraph detection</li>
<li>Encoding detection</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>EPUB Parser</h4>
<p><code>epub_parser.py</code> (5.3KB) — E-book extraction via zipfile.</p>
<ul>
<li>OPF manifest parsing</li>
<li>Chapter order preservation</li>
<li>XHTML content extraction</li>
<li>Metadata (title, author)</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>PowerPoint Parser</h4>
<p><code>ppt_parser.py</code> (3.7KB) — PPTX slide text extraction.</p>
<ul>
<li>Slide enumeration</li>
<li>Text box extraction</li>
<li>Speaker notes</li>
<li>Title/content grouping</li>
</ul>
</a>

<a href="#" class="card">
<h4>Figure Parser</h4>
<p><code>figure_parser.py</code> (12KB) — Image & figure extraction.</p>
<ul>
<li>Figure detection in PDFs</li>
<li>DOCX image extraction</li>
<li>Excel image indexing</li>
<li>Caption association</li>
<li>Vector vs. raster differentiation</li>
</ul>
</a>
</div>

<h2>Alternative Engines (Pluggable Strategies)</h2>

<p>deepdoc offers multiple parsing strategies. Choose based on your document corpus and accuracy/speed trade-off.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Engine</th><th>File</th><th>Best For</th><th>Trade-off</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Standard (pdf_parser.py)</strong></td><td>85KB</td><td>Born-digital PDFs, mixed layouts</td><td>Balanced: fast + accurate</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Docling</strong></td><td>docling_parser.py (23KB)</td><td>Complex layouts, academic papers</td><td>Slower: higher accuracy</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>MinerU</strong></td><td>mineru_parser.py (31KB)</td><td>Financial reports, structured docs</td><td>Specialized: layout-aware</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>PaddleOCR</strong></td><td>paddleocr_parser.py (23KB)</td><td>Scanned documents, Chinese text</td><td>OCR-first: multilingual</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>TCADp</strong></td><td>tcadp_parser.py (24KB)</td><td>Tables + charts</td><td>Table-focused</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>OpenDataLoader</strong></td><td>opendataloader_parser.py (16KB)</td><td>Structured extraction</td><td>JSON-oriented output</td></tr>
</table>

