<h2>Parser Decision Tree</h2>

<div class="diagram-container">
<svg viewBox="0 0 900 600" class="mermaid" data-source="parser selection logic">
graph TD
    Input["Input File"]
    
    Input -->|check ext| Format{File Format?}
    
    Format -->|.pdf| PDF["PDF Parser"]
    Format -->|.docx| DOCX["DOCX Parser"]
    Format -->|.xlsx| EXCEL["Excel Parser"]
    Format -->|.html| HTML["HTML Parser"]
    Format -->|.md| MD["Markdown Parser"]
    Format -->|.txt| TXT["Text Parser"]
    Format -->|.epub| EPUB["EPUB Parser"]
    Format -->|.pptx| PPT["PowerPoint Parser"]
    Format -->|.json| JSON["JSON Parser"]
    
    PDF -->|select engine| PDFEngine{Engine?}
    PDFEngine -->|standard| PDFStd["pdf_parser.py<br/>pdfplumber + layout"]
    PDFEngine -->|docling| PDFDocling["docling_parser.py<br/>Meta's model"]
    PDFEngine -->|mineru| PDFMineru["mineru_parser.py<br/>Vision-first"]
    PDFEngine -->|paddleocr| PDFPaddle["paddleocr_parser.py<br/>Scanned-first"]
    
    DOCX --> DocxImpl["python-docx<br/>XML walk"]
    EXCEL --> ExcelImpl["openpyxl<br/>cell iteration"]
    HTML --> HtmlImpl["BeautifulSoup<br/>DOM traversal"]
    MD --> MdImpl["markdown-it<br/>AST parsing"]
    TXT --> TxtImpl["line grouping<br/>encoding detect"]
    EPUB --> EpubImpl["zipfile + lxml<br/>OPF + XHTML"]
    PPT --> PptImpl["python-pptx<br/>slide walk"]
    JSON --> JsonImpl["json.load<br/>tree flatten"]
    
    PDFStd --> Output["Output: Sections<br/>+ optional bboxes"]
    PDFDocling --> Output
    PDFMineru --> Output
    PDFPaddle --> Output
    DocxImpl --> Output
    ExcelImpl --> Output
    HtmlImpl --> Output
    MdImpl --> Output
    TxtImpl --> Output
    EpubImpl --> Output
    PptImpl --> Output
    JsonImpl --> Output
    
    classDef inputStyle fill:#1a3a52,stroke:#58a6ff,color:#f0f6fc
    classDef decisionStyle fill:#3d3d1a,stroke:#d29922,color:#f0f6fc
    classDef pdfStyle fill:#2d5a3d,stroke:#3fb950,color:#f0f6fc
    classDef implStyle fill:#5a2d3d,stroke:#f85149,color:#f0f6fc
    classDef outputStyle fill:#3d5a2d,stroke:#d29922,color:#f0f6fc
    
    class Input inputStyle
    class Format,PDFEngine decisionStyle
    class PDF,PDFStd,PDFDocling,PDFMineru,PDFPaddle pdfStyle
    class DOCX,EXCEL,HTML,MD,TXT,EPUB,PPT,JSON,DocxImpl,ExcelImpl,HtmlImpl,MdImpl,TxtImpl,EpubImpl,PptImpl,JsonImpl implStyle
    class Output outputStyle
</svg>
</div>

<h2>Typical Parser Flow (PDF Example)</h2>

<ol style="margin-left:1.5rem;">
<li><strong>Init</strong>: Load pdfplumber, initialize LayoutRecognizer, OCR client, XGBoost model
<li><strong>Open</strong>: pdfplumber.open(file_path)
<li><strong>Iterate pages</strong>: for page in pdf.pages
<li><strong>Extract text</strong>: page.extract_text() — may return None if no text layer
<li><strong>Render image</strong>: if no text, render page at 3x zoom
<li><strong>Run layout</strong>: LayoutRecognizer(image) → bboxes with class labels
<li><strong>Assign text</strong>: Match extracted text to bboxes (spatial overlap)
<li><strong>Detect tables</strong>: For "Table" bboxes, run TableStructureRecognizer
<li><strong>Extract figures</strong>: For "Figure" bboxes, crop and save image
<li><strong>OCR fallback</strong>: For low-confidence text regions, run OCR
<li><strong>Assemble page</strong>: Collect all regions into semantic blocks (heading, text, table, figure)
<li><strong>Output</strong>: List of sections with type, text, bbox, confidence
</ol>

<h2>Error Handling Philosophy</h2>

<p><strong>Fallback chain</strong>: Gracefully degrade rather than fail.</p>

<ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;">
<li><strong>Text extraction fails</strong> → Try OCR instead
<li><strong>Layout detection fails</strong> → Output raw text (unstructured)
<li><strong>Table detection fails</strong> → Keep as text
<li><strong>Figure caption lost</strong> → Keep figure without caption
<li><strong>Model loading fails (local)</strong> → Download from HuggingFace
<li><strong>Remote DLA fails</strong> → Fall back to local ONNX
<li><strong>Low confidence</strong> → Include with confidence flag, let downstream decide
</ul>

<h2>Performance Characteristics</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Parser</th><th>Speed</th><th>Accuracy</th><th>Scanned PDFs</th><th>Multilingual</th></tr>
<tr><td>pdf_parser.py (standard)</td><td>Fast</td><td>High</td><td>Good (with OCR)</td><td>Good</td></tr>
<tr><td>docling_parser.py</td><td>Medium</td><td>Very High</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Good</td></tr>
<tr><td>mineru_parser.py</td><td>Medium</td><td>Very High</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Fair</td></tr>
<tr><td>paddleocr_parser.py</td><td>Medium</td><td>High</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent (80+ langs)</td></tr>
<tr><td>docx_parser.py</td><td>Very Fast</td><td>Excellent</td><td>N/A</td><td>Good</td></tr>
<tr><td>html_parser.py</td><td>Very Fast</td><td>Good</td><td>N/A</td><td>Good</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Resume Parser (Specialized)</h2>

<p>Directory: <code>parser/resume/</code> — Dedicated resume extraction with field detection (contact, experience, skills, education).</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>

<p>The parser layer abstracts away format specifics. Whether your input is a scanned PDF, a spreadsheet, or HTML, deepdoc's parsers extract semantic content and pass it to the vision and chunking layers. Multi-engine support lets you optimize for accuracy, speed, or language coverage.</p>

